{:id "0058-lab-flick-ui"
 ;; 2026-11-18: trimmed before its first run (no debug line, no replay
 ;; key), after the board showed what a page-sized order costs.
 ;; Its first run was cut short by a container restart two minutes into
 ;; the build, after the plan ($1.66); its second by another restart 22
 ;; minutes into the build, with all six files written. That work
 ;; survived on disk and passes `bb test` and `bb lab:e2e` (33 steps), so
 ;; this third run is a resume, as the board's was: the builder applies
 ;; the saved diff and the review station reads it. The plan station is
 ;; replaced by the foreman's note (:engines).
 :title "Lab flick, the page: 'Which?' reads your line back two ways and your style moves toward the one you pick"
 :lupa/deps #{"0053-lab-flick" "0059-lab-flick-turn"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md, 'How people and agents drive it', and H5
        and H8 in docs/product/lab-notebook.md. The pure exam is lab.flick
        (orders 0053 and 0059). Put it on the page: on request the lab
        reads the current line back as A (your style now) and as B (one
        step along one axis), you flick toward the one you like, and your
        style point moves. Never unprompted."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "public/lab/index.html"
         "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"
         "src/halfahead/lab/flick.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/flick_test.cljc"]
 :engines {:plan {:engine :exec
                  :cmd ["cat" "../../../out/foreman/0058-plan.md"]}}
 :design "RESUME (2026-11-18). The last run built all of what follows
          before the container restarted under it. Its whole diff is
          saved at ../../../out/foreman/0058-lab-flick-ui.patch, relative
          to the worktree's root; on it the foreman ran `bb test` (no
          failures) and `bb lab:e2e` (33 steps, all passing, on WebGL2).
          To build is to apply that patch (`git apply`), run `bb test`,
          and change nothing that works. The rest of this design says
          what the patch holds and what the review judges it against.
          lab.main and index.html: a 'Which?' button in the bar and Ctrl+/
            ask for one exam on the current text (the button is disabled
            with no text or with reduced motion).
            The learner's state (lab.learn) is kept in the page and
            remembered per viewer in localStorage (every access in
            try/catch). Its point is the lab's style point. One new pure
            function decides that, with a test on both hosts:
            (flick/resume state point) -> state when its point is point
            (or state is nil: then (learn/start point)), else the learner
            started again at point (learn/start point). The page calls it
            when an exam is asked for, with the point of the style in
            force (a named style's point, the style Auto reads at that
            moment, or the board's point under Mine).
            Then (flick/offer state text pace). nil: the chip says
            'Nothing more to tell apart on this line' for two seconds and
            nothing else happens (that is how an exam ends). Otherwise
            the exam runs on (flick/phases offer): a chip reads 'A' while
            reading A plays, 'B' while B plays, then 'A or B?' with two
            buttons. ArrowLeft or the A button chooses A, ArrowRight or
            the B button chooses B; Escape at any time cancels and
            changes nothing. Each reading plays through the lab's
            read-back path with that reading's point as the style (dress
            included). The text cannot be edited while an exam runs.
            On a choice the state becomes (flick/decide offer choice),
            the style becomes Mine at the state's point (the board's XY
            dot shows it) and the state is stored. The chip is an
            aria-live region, so a screen reader hears 'A', 'B', 'A or
            B?'.
            The style picked is remembered per viewer as well (today
            only the point is, so a reload falls back to Auto and a
            learned style is not in force): a reload starts in the style
            last picked, Mine included. Existing browser checks that
            count on Auto at the start must still pass: give them a
            fresh page with empty storage where they need one.
            window.__lab.flick() -> {phase axis pointA pointB flicks
            point} as plain data; phase is null when no exam runs.
          e2e/lab.mjs, a new step 'flick' (?reveal=3, on a page with
          empty storage): type 'I loooove this (honestly). But maybe
          not. Ship it!' and wait for rest; Ctrl+/: flick().phase goes a,
          then b, then choose (wait on the data, not on the clock), and
          pointA and pointB differ on exactly the axis reported; press
          ArrowRight: flick().flicks is 1, point equals pointB, and the
          style picker shows Mine; Ctrl+/ then Escape: flicks and point
          are unchanged; two more exams choosing the option with the
          higher energy: point.energy has not fallen; reload: the point
          and the flick count are kept and the picker still shows Mine;
          pick Elegant and reload: the picker shows Elegant; then with a
          stored state whose steps are all below 1/16 (write it to
          storage and reload), Ctrl+/ shows 'Nothing more to tell apart
          on this line' and flick().phase stays null. Screenshot
          out/lab/flick.png during a choose phase. The step says which
          backend it ran on.
          docs/LAB.md: a short section 'The flick': what it asks, how it
          ends, and what it can learn from a line (H8: speed and bounce
          from any line; flourish only where the line gives it something
          to do; warmth not yet)."
 :acceptance
 ["flick/resume's test, on both hosts; `bb test` stays green"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the flick step and every existing step;
   out/lab/flick.png for the foreman"]
 :non-goals
 ["Never start an exam unprompted; no telemetry; nothing leaves the device"
  "No change to lab.flick beyond adding resume; none to lab.learn,
   reading, pace, marks, score, gestures, synth, dress, the board's
   pads, the renderer or the director; do not edit the schema"
  "No debug overlay line and no replay key in this order"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/lab/flick.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/flick_test.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/board.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/main.cljs" "public/lab/index.html"
           "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
